cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VitalFi in research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "VitalFi: Wi-Fi–based life detection under rubble"
abstract: >-
  VitalFi is an open-source experimental Android application and companion Python
  tooling for research on device-free Wi-Fi sensing in search-and-rescue scenarios.
  It monitors RSSI fluctuations from a local 2.4 GHz access point, applies digital
  signal processing on-device, and estimates breathing-related activity with a
  bearing/distance hypothesis shown on an offline 2D/3D radar UI. Results are
  heuristic and must not replace professional rescue equipment or protocols.
